# Install releases into /Applications

Whenever you ship a new BookmarkX version (commit + DMG + GitHub Release), also update the local installed app so the Desktop shortcut keeps launching the latest build.

## Required steps (every release)

1. Build/package as usual (`./Scripts/package-dmg.sh <version>` or equivalent Release build).
2. Install into Applications with **replace app only**:

```bash
./Scripts/install-to-applications.sh
# or explicitly:
./Scripts/install-to-applications.sh /path/to/BookmarkX.app
```

3. Confirm `/Applications/BookmarkX.app` reports the new `CFBundleShortVersionString`.

## Hard rules — data safety

- **Do** replace `/Applications/BookmarkX.app` (and recreate the Desktop alias if it is broken).
- **Do not** delete, reset, move, merge, rewrite, or “clean up” anything under:
  - `~/Library/Containers/com.williamyang.BookmarkX/` (sandboxed app data — **this is what Applications uses**)
  - `~/Library/Application Support/BookmarkX/` (legacy / non-sandbox copy — may still hold recent edits)
  - credentials / login session / SQLite / folders / bookmarks / settings
- **Do not** run SQL against the live DB as part of install/upgrade unless the user explicitly asks to repair/restore data.
- Prefer `ditto` / the install script over dragging from DMG when automating; quit BookmarkX first if it is running, then copy **only** the `.app` bundle.
- Never call `pruneEmptyFolders` (or any folder wipe / full reclassify) as a side effect of installing or launching after upgrade.

## Why two data locations exist

Sandboxed `/Applications/BookmarkX.app` stores data in the **container** path. Some Debug / older runs may write to `~/Library/Application Support/BookmarkX/`. Replacing the `.app` does not delete either store, but launching Applications after install shows the container DB — folders created in the legacy store can look “lost”. Treat both paths as user data; do not erase either.

## Why

The Desktop shortcut points at `/Applications/BookmarkX.app`. Shipping only a GitHub DMG leaves the installed app stale, so the shortcut opens an old version.
